from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
p=Path('.tmp/pages-download-review')
(p/'review.md').write_text('''# Independent authenticated artifact ZIP download review

Reviewed deployment/download package, tests and final deployment README on base 7c4bc00 against the authenticated observation/artifact boundary, spec15 bounded acquisition and the official Actions artifact download contract. No implementation edits, real API actions or public deployment.

No blocking finding. The API request is fixed to the validated artifact ID ZIP route with bearer authorization. Exactly one 302 Location must identify HTTPS Azure Blob Storage with no userinfo, explicit port, fragment or unsupported host; a separate storage connection omits bearer/cookie/referrer and accepts no further redirect. Size/digest are independently supplied from authenticated metadata. MIME, identity encoding, framing, exact byte count and digest are checked; the parent rechecks output length and SHA-256. Accepted data is at most 256MiB, with one extra byte read to detect overflow. ZIP interpretation remains a separate verifier.

Independent 5 tests passed normally and with python -O using real loopback HTTP (connection factory substituted, TLS not tested). Additional real HTTP probes accepted complete chunked content, rejected a missing terminating chunk, and rejected missing/duplicate Location before any second request. An actual -I worker IPC probe preserved the original bytes with fetch stubbed, kept credentials out of argv, and rejected oversized/invalid worker stdin with nonzero exit and no stdout/stderr. A real sleeping child triggered sanitized timeout failure under a configured 0.1-second wait. Startup/scheduling/kill-wait and parent hashing overhead do not give a hard real-time guarantee.

Final README accurately discloses host buffering/IPC, isolated child limits, no retry/extraction/overwrite and no eligibility implication. Its initial '256MiB read' wording was corrected to accepted bytes plus the sentinel read. Removal of an unused import after the test runs has no behavior impact. Root's production HTTPS/real-GitHub download evidence is separate from this review's local/stubbed tests; I do not claim independently executing that network fetch.

Storage provider restrictions fail closed if GitHub changes hosts. Authentication of size/digest, total transaction remaining budget, candidate content validation, main freshness, writer-state/permission and publication/LKG remain outside this transport. No signed URL or credential from live service was captured in these review artifacts.

Official contract: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/artifacts#download-an-artifact (authenticated endpoint supplies a short-lived 302 ZIP download URL; consulted in this review sequence). The observed Azure provider restriction is an implementation-supported subset, not a permanent universal REST guarantee.
''',encoding='utf8',newline='\n')
for name in ['tools/site/deployment/download/__init__.py','tools/site/deployment/download/worker.py','tools/site/test_download.py','tools/site/deployment/README.md']:
 f=p/'source'/name;f.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);f.write_bytes(Path(name).read_bytes())
rows=[]
for f in sorted(p.rglob('*')):
 if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json':
  b=f.read_bytes();rows.append(dict(path=f.relative_to(p).as_posix(),bytes=len(b),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()))
(p/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(files=rows),indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8');print(len(rows),sum(r['bytes'] for r in rows))
